I added the cron, new lang variables are needed:
```

$subject = get_lang('UserRequestWaitingForAction');
$content = sprintf(
                get_lang('TheUserXIsWaitingForAnActionGoHereX'),
                $userInfo['complete_name'],
                $link
            );
```

@NicoDucou I've fixed that, but URLs should *always* be out of the translation term, because they tend to change over time (not based on the language but based on some regulation change or external site change).
Once they have been translated, it is *very* difficult to go and change all the different versions of the translated string.
In this case I understand the intent is to give a different URL for each language, but I think that's a bad ID. We can point to the neutral second link only.
